  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n~\nServices\nPerformance audit\n\n// Service\n\nPerformance audit \n\nA measured list of what is slow, why, and what each fix is worth.\n\nPrice\nFrom €3,200\nTimeline\n1 week\nStart this project\n\nOpens the contact form with this service picked. Nothing is sent yet.\n\n// Scope\n\nI profile your product on real devices and on your real traffic, then hand you a ranked list: the change, the expected gain and the effort. The first three fixes come as pull requests.\n\nIncludes\n\nField and lab measurements\nRanked findings with numbers\nThree fixes as pull requests\nA budget your CI can enforce\n\n// How it runs\n\nFrom the first note to the handover. \n\n01\nDay 1\n\nField data\n\nI read what your real visitors get: the 75th percentile for LCP, INP and CLS, split by page type and device.\n\n02\nDays 2 to 3\n\nProfiling\n\nThe slowest five journeys, traced on a mid-range Android and a three year old laptop. Every finding gets a cause, not a guess.\n\n03\nDay 4\n\nRanked report\n\nOne list, ordered by what each fix is worth: the change, the expected gain in milliseconds and the effort in days.\n\n04\nDay 5\n\nThree fixes\n\nThe top three land as pull requests, with before and after traces, plus a budget file your CI can enforce.\n\n// Questions\n\nAsked about this service. \n01\nDo you need production access?\n\nRead access to the repository and to your analytics is enough. I never need customer data.\n\n02\nWhat if nothing is slow?\n03\nCan you fix everything you find?\n\n// Other services\n\nFrom €9,500\nFrontend build\nYour product's interface, from the first component to the production deploy.\nFrom €12,000\nDesign system\nOne set of tokens and components your whole team actually uses.\nFrom €6,400 a month\nTeam embed\nA senior frontend developer inside your team, three days a week.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n17:01 CEST\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.\n\nEdit Content",
